    <string name="speech_consent_title">"External speech recognition"</string>
    <string name="speech_consent_message">"The installed speech recognizer, usually Google, may record and upload microphone audio. The keyboard has no Internet permission, but the recognizer can send audio.\n\nTyping and correction work locally without this feature. You can revoke approval in dictation settings. Allow external speech recognition?"</string>
    <string name="speech_consent_allow">"Allow external speech"</string>
    <string name="speech_consent_decline">"Keep typing local"</string>
    <string name="speech_ready">"Approval saved. Tap the microphone again to dictate."</string>
    <string name="privacy_summary">"Local typing\nTyping, correction and emoji search run on this device. There is no Internet permission, account, analytics, developer server or background GitHub connection. GitHub hosts the source, not a typing service.\n\nOptional dictation\nAn external recognizer, usually Google, may record and upload audio after separate approval and microphone permission. You can revoke approval in dictation settings.\n\nAndroid warnings\nA keyboard can receive what you type. Android’s keyboard warning describes this capability; it is not by itself a malware finding. Open source does not guarantee a safe APK. Review Play Protect, signature and tampering alerts separately. This preview has no trusted production signing identity or independent security guarantee.\n\nLocal storage\nSettings, recent emoji, dictionaries and an optional font stay in private app storage. Clipboard offers are off by default. There is no typing-history database. The app receiving your text has its own privacy policy."</string>
